# ORCA frontend configuration.
#
# Copy to .env.local for a local run against a deployed API, or leave absent to
# use the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts forwards /api to http://localhost:8080,
# override with ORCA_API).

# Base URL of the Go API. Leave unset in development so requests go through the
# dev proxy on a single origin. In production set it to the Render URL, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://orca-api.onrender.com
#
# This is a *build* variable, not a runtime one: it is read when `npm run build`
# writes dist/, so it has to be set in the host's build environment (Vercel and
# Render both inject build-time variables from the service's settings).
#
# Unset means same-origin: the bundle calls /api on whatever host served it,
# which is correct only behind a reverse proxy that forwards /api to the Go
# service. Without that proxy the deployed site requests itself, gets HTML or a
# 404 where JSON was expected, and shows an empty map with no error anywhere —
# the same class of silent failure as the dev proxy pointing at a dead port.
# Note this is *not* the dev proxy target: `npm run dev` works with this unset
# because Vite forwards /api itself, and a static build has nothing doing that.
#
# VITE_API_BASE=
